    "section": "Postactinoid elements: You have seen that elements with atomic number greater than 92 are called 'Transuranium'. Elements from atomic number 93 to 103 now are included in actinoid series and those from 104 to 118 are called as postactinoid elements. The postactinoid elements that are known so far are transition metals. They are included as postactinoids because similar to actinoid elements, they can be synthesized in the nuclear reactions. So far, nine postactinoid elements have been synthesized. It is difficult to study their chemistry owing their short half-lives. For example, element 112 has a half-life of only 2.8 x 10&lt;sup&gt;-4&lt;/sup&gt; seconds.",
